\section*{Quasipolynomial trace samples for arbitrary symbols}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 122; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that worst-case trace reconstruction has quasipolynomial sample bounds with logarithm $O((\log n)^3(1+\log\log(2n))^6)$ at fixed retention, including general exactly observed symbols, without an algorithmic guarantee.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Each source symbol is retained independently with probability $p\in(0,1]$, and the output consists of the retained symbols in order. The decoder knows the length $n$ and retention probability $p$ and receives independent traces. For every $x\in\{0,1\}^n$ its reconstruction success must be at least $2/3$. For every $n\ge2$, the claimed worst-case trace sample bound is
\[
 N\le\exp\bigl(O(p^{-1}(\log n)^3(1+\log\log(2n))^6)\bigr).
\]
The constants are absolute. For $q=1-p>0$ and $\mathcal X=1+\log n/(1+\log(1/q))$, the refined bound is
\[
 \log N=O(p^{-1}(\log n)\mathcal X^2(1+\log\mathcal X)^6).
\]
For each fixed $\varepsilon>0$, $q\le n^{-\varepsilon}$ therefore permits polynomially many traces. Exact observation of retained symbols also allows general alphabets. This is a sample-complexity claim, with no comparable running-time assertion.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 122; 2026-10-05), gap probes use compact spectral masks and a latest-anchor induction to keep a signal during shuffling and scale transfer. Radial compactification and stopping-stage interpolation produce separation of trace laws; the argument then reduces general symbols to the detected binary distinction.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
The bound is for the number of deletion traces with known retention and exactly observed symbols; it asserts no efficient reconstruction method. Complete coverage of the displayed statistical guarantee is not established by this catalogue, and the claim remains partial.

\subsection{Formal verification}
No Lean formalization is listed at this snapshot for manuscript 1 (family 122; 2026-10-05).

This site has not executed the Lean code. Described statement coverage is not an independent proof check.

\subsection{Status caveat}
The manuscripts were produced by an internal OpenAI model. OpenAI cautions that results without formalization can contain mistakes. This site has not independently checked the proofs; the label records the scope of OpenAI's claim.

